    {
      "id": "text-on-image-13",
      "type": "text-on-image",
      "content": {
        "image": {
          "src": "https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6465c08bc2eb8d26649eade8/65d754bed520cd31450b357a_WasteminsterBG.BTS2.jpg",
          "alt": ""
        },
        "parts": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "heading": "Production",
            "body": "We believe that comedy can be a powerful tool to help tell some of the saddest stories in our world. That's why we created mannequin versions of Boris Johnson and Michael Gove that represent them, but that also introduce some distance to these real politicians. After all, they are only dummies. Our intention was not to ridicule politicians, but to place their dummy-personas in a direct conflict with the invisible consequences of their own actions.",
            "dark": true
          },
          {
            "kind": "film",
            "film": {
              "provider": "youtube",
              "id": "1OL8FxUwlT0",
              "poster": "https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6465c08bc2eb8d26649eade8/65d7552e41e4da38f2b55af6_WasteminsterCover.BTS.jpg",
              "ratio": "16:9"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "spaceBefore": "4-5"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote-14",
      "type": "quote",
      "content": {
        "quote": "\"We didn’t want to put words into Boris’s mouth so we went through hours of interviews and speeches by Boris and the government where plastic pollution and the environment were discussed and quotes were extracted. All statements in the film were made by Boris and the government.\"",
        "cite": "Directors Jorik Dozy & Sil van der Woerd"
      },
      "padTop": "4-5",
      "padBottom": "4-5"
    },
    {
      "id": "text-15",
      "type": "text",
      "content": {
        "heading": "1.8 Million KG",
        "body": "To visualize how much trash the UK exports daily, we started with the latest real world data. In 2020, the UK exported an average of 1.8 million kilograms of plastic waste every single day.\n\nWe researched the most common items found in household plastic waste, which resulted in 150 different pieces - plastic bags, coffee cups, etc. These were then modeled in 3d with various crushed or damaged variations to add to the realism. Using Daniel Webb and Dr. Julie Schneider’s research of their ‘Everyday Plastic’ project, we fine tuned the balance between all the items and how frequent they are found in our trash. We then looked up the average weight of each of the 150 items and concluded that it takes on average, 37 plastic items to make up 1KG of plastic waste. \n\n‍\n\nThat makes the daily export of UK plastic waste a total of 67.7 million pieces.\n\n‍\n\nThe talented team at Method & Madness under leadership of CG Director Alex Scollay built a digital Downing Street set using satellite imagery onto which we unleashed a computer simulation. To define the actual size of the waste pile, we combined 1,000 plastic items into a single, large ball. We then dropped 67.7 thousand of those balls onto our digital set, giving us a realistic representation of the actual daily volume. In total, the two minute film required roughly 14,600 hours of render time, or 20 months, to create the final shots. The CO2 emitted by our render farm was compensated for."
      },
      "padBottom": "4-5"
    },
